abstract: >-
  This package contains the MATLAB and Python code that reproduces the
  figures and the headline numerical claims of the paper, including the
  300-configuration coarse-grained generalized-second-law sweep, the
  Cherenkov phase-matching scaling k_RR * delta3 = const, and the
  diagnostic spectral-entropy and entropy-production-efficiency
  computations. The dispersion convention is the integrability-consistent
  anomalous-dispersion form (+i delta3 d^3/dtau^3); the original
  submission's Boltzmann thermal-tail fit is withdrawn and replaced by a
  positive identification of the radiation as a coherent phase-matched
  Cherenkov resonance.
keywords:
  - analog gravity
  - optical event horizon
  - nonequilibrium thermodynamics
  - generalized second law
  - soliton fission
  - resonant radiation
  - Cherenkov phase matching
  - GNLSE
